Do not interpose `__cxa_throw` from libnixutil.

Determinate Nix links an interposer into libnixutil that aborts the
process when anything throws a `std::logic_error` (DeterminateSystems
4cfdfb29, "Abort when throwing std::logic_error"). libnixutil exports
the symbol, so it replaces `__cxa_throw` for the whole process, not
only for Nix.

For `nix` that is a policy on its own code. In an embedder it reaches
every throw: huggorm raises a Python `ValueError` by throwing
`std::invalid_argument`, nanobind and libstdc++ throw `out_of_range`,
and each one aborted the interpreter. The suite died in
test_a_partly_applied_builtin_is_the_third_shape. The abort is chosen
when the interposer is compiled, so a caller cannot turn it off.

The interposer stays in the tree; libutil no longer links it.

--- a/src/libutil/meson.build
+++ b/src/libutil/meson.build
@@ -136,10 +136,6 @@
 
 subdir('nix-meson-build-support/common')
 
-if have_cxa_throw
-  deps_other += cxa_throw_dep
-endif
-
 sources = [ config_priv_h ] + files(
   'archive.cc',
   'args.cc',
